# ── dt-evals credentials (copy to .env, never commit the real file) ──────────
# .env is gitignored. `dt-evals doctor` can also write DT_API_TOKEN here for you.

# Dynatrace environment that holds your agents' GenAI spans + receives the eval
# results. For the workshop this is the SHARED tenant (see evals/DECISIONS.md) —
# the same tenant you set as DT_TENANT_URL for the platform install.
#   Required token scopes:  storage:spans:read  +  storage:events:write
DT_ENV_URL=https://YOUR-ENV.live.dynatrace.com
DT_API_TOKEN=dt0c01.XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

# ── Judge LLM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LEAVE COMMENTED on a workshop Codespace. The room-password proxy (ISI-6996)
# dispenses a per-attendee virtual key, and run-dt-eval.sh injects the judge
# baseUrl from WORKSHOP_LLM_BASE_URL_NOV1 (the proxy endpoint) into the rendered
# .dt-eval.yaml. run-dt-eval.sh also auto-maps OPENAI_API_KEY from the dispensed
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY / LLM_API_KEY, so nothing here is needed.
#
# NOTE: dt-evals takes its judge baseUrl from the YAML, NOT OPENAI_BASE_URL — so
# OPENAI_BASE_URL below is inert for dt-evals. Only set OPENAI_API_KEY to a direct
# key to deliberately BYPASS the proxy.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=${DEEPSEEK_API_KEY:-${LLM_API_KEY}}
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/v1   # inert for dt-evals; proxy baseUrl comes from the YAML

# ── Alternatives (pick ONE; comment the DeepSeek lines above) ────────────────
# Real OpenAI  — drop OPENAI_BASE_URL and set judge.provider/model accordingly:
#   OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Anthropic    — set judge.provider: anthropic, judge.model: claude-sonnet-4-6:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
